legacy-peer-deps=true
# Peer-dep strictness introduced in npm 7 doesn't match this tree's reality:
# runtime works with the current combo (vite 8 + typescript 7 + @vitejs/plugin-react 6 + vitest 4),
# but typescript-eslint 8.x and kimi-plugin-inspect-react 1.0.3 have older peer ranges
# that conflict with the newer versions. The runtime behavior is correct; only the
# install-time check fails. Vercel + GitHub Actions' `npm ci` both honor this flag.
